Subsistence farming is understood to mean the one whose objective is to produce sufficient food to exclusively meet the needs of the farmer and his family group.
Subsistence farming is a simple, generally organic practice that combines the use of stored seeds originating in the ecological region with crop rotation or other comparatively simple methods to maximise production.
Historically, much of the main activity of farmers was subsistence agriculture, which is still practised in many developing countries.
Subcultures bring together individuals with similar ideas and feelings of marginalization by social standards and gives them the possibility of generating a sense of identity.
