Traits that distinguish a subculture can be linguistic, aesthetic, sexual, geographical or related to religion or politics, or a mixture of factors.
It is frequent that the members of a subculture exhibit traits of their belonging to it by resorting to the distinctive and symbolic use of style, such as fashions, gestures and squirring.
