The proteins present in the leaves and legumes would have been the source of plant resources of easier access, but they are not easily digestible for primates like us, unless they are cooked.
On the other hand, animal-derived foods (ants, termites, eggs) are easy to digest while providing a large number of proteins that contain all the essential amino acids.
In short, it should come as no surprise if our own predecessors solved their “protein problems” in the same way as savannah chimpanzees today.
